This product bundles word-frequency data derived from the following projects:

  wordfreq <https://github.com/rspeer/wordfreq/>
    Copyright (c) 2014–2024 Robyn Speer and contributors.
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    The data exposed by wordfreq combines multiple corpora distributed under
    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 and other attributed source
    licenses. See the wordfreq repository for full upstream attribution.

  OpenCC Python <https://github.com/yichen0831/opencc-python/>
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
    Used to convert wordfreq's `zh` data into Simplified (Hans) and
    Traditional (Hant) variants.

The derived files in `crates/language-identifier/src/data/lexicon_*.txt` are
distributed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> in keeping with the
upstream data licenses.

When the optional `ml-fasttext` cargo feature is enabled, callers point the
library at Meta/FAIR's `lid.176.bin` model file at runtime. The library
does not bundle that model, but consumers redistributing it should
preserve the upstream attribution:

  fastText / lid.176 <https://fasttext.cc/docs/en/language-identification.html>
    Joulin, Grave, Bojanowski & Mikolov, "Bag of Tricks for Efficient Text
    Classification" (2016) and "FastText.zip: Compressing text
    classification models" (2016).
    Model weights distributed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
    3.0 <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/>.

The rest of this repository (Rust source code, documentation, build
configuration) is distributed under the MIT OR Apache-2.0 dual license as
declared in the workspace `Cargo.toml`.
